WEBVTT

00:05:29.196 --> 00:05:31.796
We like rainy days and tragic drama

00:05:31.836 --> 00:05:33.116
and cherry blossoms,

00:05:33.116 --> 00:05:35.836
which we celebrate
over equally lovely flowers

00:05:35.876 --> 00:05:37.876
partly because they die young.

00:05:39.076 --> 00:05:42.076
Philosophers call that
the paradox of tragedy.

00:05:42.876 --> 00:05:45.516
Why do we sometimes welcome sorrow

00:05:45.556 --> 00:05:47.916
when the rest of the time
we will quite naturally

00:05:47.956 --> 00:05:50.156
do anything we can to avoid it?

00:05:51.996 --> 00:05:54.996
There's actually a scholarly debate
raging over this question,

00:05:55.036 --> 00:05:57.156
but I have come to believe

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.236
that really, what we are craving,

00:05:59.236 --> 00:06:00.516
at bottom,